# What `tauri dev` must not restart the app for. Its watcher leaves out
# .gitignore'd entries only at the top of src-tauri; below that, only this file
# filters (and, once it exists, the CLI's own list: node_modules/, target/,
# gen/, Cargo.lock).
#
# A development host builds a remote agent on demand when it connects to a
# machine that has none of its build (`remote_link::build_locally`). srt-win,
# which travels with a Windows build, is built in its own crate directory, so
# its cargo output would restart the app halfway through the connection that
# asked for it.
vendor/srt-win/target/
remote-agents/
